    "hash": "3b84c962082583c471da0e1769305d1d52376e91915e7a9144f24ff56e860f6d",
    "summary_one_sentence": "Co-directed by Billie Eilish and James Cameron, this immersive 3D concert film captures the multi-Grammy winner's electrifying arena performances during her sold-out world tour.",
    "summary_short": "Co-directed by Billie Eilish and James Cameron, Billie Eilish – Hit Me Hard and Soft: The Tour (Live in 3D) offers fans an unprecedented front-row view of the superstar's sold-out global tour. Filmed using cutting-edge 3D technology at the Co-op Live arena in Manchester, the concert spectacle captures Eilish performing signature tracks alongside her brother and collaborator, Finneas. Beyond high-energy musical setpieces, the film integrates handheld stage cameras and candid backstage moments to redefine the modern concert documentary experience.",
    "summary_long": "Billie Eilish – Hit Me Hard and Soft: The Tour (Live in 3D) chronicles the boundary-pushing concert tour supporting Billie Eilish's acclaimed studio album. Co-directed alongside legendary filmmaker James Cameron, the film opens with a time-lapse of the massive stage production being constructed inside Manchester's Co-op Live arena. As the lights drop, Eilish takes the stage inside a floating illuminated cube, launching into a dynamic setlist that balances intense anthems with deeply emotional acoustic ballads. Joined onstage by her brother and producer Finneas, Eilish delivers stripped-back renditions of iconic tracks while taking advantage of bespoke 3D camera setups. Throughout the performance, Eilish uses handheld 3D cameras directly on stage to offer fans raw, direct-to-lens perspectives of her set. Interspersed between the high-octane musical numbers are quiet, reflective moments, including a serene instance where she requests complete silence from the arena crowd to capture live ambient audio. The film's immersive visual technology pulls the audience directly into the crowd, highlighting the emotional bond between Eilish and her fanbase. Devoted listeners and concertgoers share poignant reflections on what her music represents, grounding the spectacle in genuine connection. As the concert culminates in a triumph of light, sound, and visual artistry, the movie captures both the explosive scale of arena pop and the delicate interiority of Eilish's songwriting. Ultimately, the documentary stands as a groundbreaking fusion of live musical passion and state-of-the-art 3D cinema.",
    "synopsis": "Billie Eilish – Hit Me Hard and Soft: The Tour (Live in 3D) brings one of pop music's most celebrated modern icons to the big screen in a groundbreaking concert documentary co-directed by Eilish and Academy Award-winning director James Cameron. Filmed during her sold-out world tour, the movie delivers an all-access, VIP perspective into Eilish's electrifying live performances. Utilizing state-of-the-art 3D technology, the cinematic experience places viewers directly alongside fans in the arena and up close on stage with Eilish and her brother, Finneas. From massive, high-energy hits to intimate acoustic moments, the film captures the emotional depth, raw energy, and artistic innovation that define Eilish's hit-filled tour, serving as a landmark celebration of live music and visual storytelling.",
